        <mxCell id="padNote" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#333333;" value="fast path: 32 trajectories stacked into a [T_max, 32] grid and swept together;&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;padded cells carry ρ̂ = ĉ = δ = 0, so each column is exactly the standalone&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;recurrence — the accumulator never crosses a trajectory boundary (diagram 06)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="360" x="1060" y="540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="frame5" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#D79B00;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fontColor=#D79B00;" value="(5) outputs → losses" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="780" x="40" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=11;" value="value target vs_t (detached)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="300" x="70" y="735" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="o2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=11;" value="advantage A_t = ρ̂_t·( r̃_t + γ·vs_{t+1} − V_t )&lt;br&gt;note: bootstraps on the TARGET vs_{t+1}, not V_{t+1}" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="300" x="70" y="820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l1" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=11;" value="value loss = mean over N of ( v_θ(s_t) − vs_t )²" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="320" x="460" y="735" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l2" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=11;" value="NeuRD policy loss — A_t scales the logit update of every legal action (β = 2.5, diagram 03)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="320" x="460" y="820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cons" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;fontSize=10;align=left;spacing=8;" value="Reading the clips:&lt;br&gt;• π = μ (on-policy): all ratios = 1, nothing clips, the sum telescopes → vs_t = Σ_{s≥t} r̃_s — the plain Monte-Carlo return of the transformed game (γ = 1)&lt;br&gt;• ρ̄ sets the FIXED POINT: v-trace estimates V^{π_ρ̄} with π_ρ̄ ∝ min(ρ̄·μ, π) — between V^μ (ρ̄ → 0) and V^π (ρ̄ → ∞); ρ̄ = 1 keeps it close to V^π while μ ≈ π&lt;br&gt;• c̄ does NOT move the fixed point — it only shortens how far a future δ propagates backward: bias-free variance control&lt;br&gt;• every output here is a constant for backprop (detached) — gradients flow only through the two losses on the left" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="580" x="860" y="700" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
